  "accepted_scope": {
    "constant_scalar_centre_mixing": "The reviewed fixed physical-view classes force A=cI8. The original fixed source/Y-tail class and the bounded canonical-interval extension have separate premises. The 63-minor and two-basis arguments are exact. No arbitrary native-path, query/scatter, wrapper, or operator-valued-matrix conclusion follows.",
    "direct_capture": "Rank sum at least 62 for one unwarped carrier per source on an increasing subspace chain and one direct complete common-frame capture per centre row. Extra carriers, partial queries, and operator-valued codes are excluded; pair coding violates the carrier premise.",
    "dyadic_observations": "The actual BD=13I data force rank[B;M]=16 when M is dyadic and MD is a dyadic two-sided unit. The full-null family bounds total fixed linear observation rank under the stated output partition; it does not bound scratch or native children. The rank-eight rational alternative and integral-domain coefficient-ring consequence retain their exact unit and rank hypotheses.",
    "payload_query_spans": "Under scalar plain interfaces and gates, each I+uQv query with scalar u,v adds at most one scalar source/response direction. Every non-scalar payload map counts, including rank-zero address maps; r-direction blocks count r. The actual line and proposed matched-plane source ranks are 112 at positive tensor depth. Mixed-plane endpoints need at least n such queries on n fields."
  },
